<ProjectLayout slug="pa-job-market">
  <Fragment slot="intro">
    <section class="section">
      <div class="narrow">
        <h2 class="section-title">In short</h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <ul>
            <li><b>For new PAs.</b> It answers what a graduating physician assistant wants to know: which specialties hire new grads, what they pay, where the jobs are, and how long the search takes.</li>
            <li><b>Data from NCCPA,</b> the board that certifies every PA in the US: its 2025 workforce profile, its 2024 survey of newly certified PAs, and its reports by specialty and by state. Every number is kept with its source table in the repo.</li>
            <li><b>The charts:</b> an interactive US map, pay by specialty and experience, where new grads land compared with where they want to work, first-job salaries, the job search and debt. See them in the <a href="/research/pa-job-market">write-up</a>.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </Fragment>
</ProjectLayout>
